WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.374 --> 00:00:03.222
- 'Cause once you give up,
you're just waiting to die.

00:00:03.222 --> 00:00:05.383
You know you want nice, quiet,
stay at home with grandma,

00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.569
pour another glass of water,
put her false teeth in it.

00:00:08.569 --> 00:00:11.241
If that way one and one can equal three.

00:00:11.241 --> 00:00:13.100
That it doesn't matter who you are,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.225
your dreams can come true.

00:00:14.225 --> 00:00:16.184
Everybody's in one business.

00:00:16.184 --> 00:00:17.845
The people business.

00:00:17.845 --> 00:00:20.060
It says music business.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.528
It doesn't just say music.

00:00:21.528 --> 00:00:23.565
Give me a new maze every day.

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:25.722
My most profitable
venture is Gene Simmons.

00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:27.071
I want it.

00:00:27.071 --> 00:00:27.970
I want it...I want it all.

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.660
We all have our crosses to bear,

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.890
so (bleep) what, get over it.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.404
- He's a rock star, singer,
songwriter, entrepreneur,

00:00:36.404 --> 00:00:37.865
and television personality.

00:00:37.865 --> 00:00:41.941
- He was known as the demon
and the co-lead singer of KISS.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.823
- He has an estimated net worth
of over 300 million dollars.

00:00:45.823 --> 00:00:47.441
- He's Gene Simmons and here are

00:00:47.441 --> 00:00:49.941
his top ten rules for success.

00:00:52.764 --> 00:00:55.864
- Because you want inspiration,
look to your mother.

00:00:55.864 --> 00:00:57.136
You bet.

00:00:57.136 --> 00:01:00.083
Don't listen to the self help
gurus and the people stuff,

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:01.395
even though I get paid a lot of

00:01:01.395 --> 00:01:03.279
money to do this stuff myself,

00:01:03.279 --> 00:01:04.217
(audience laughs)

00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:06.704
turn around and look at your mom.

00:01:06.704 --> 00:01:08.020
That's the most inspiration,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.212
that's the reason you should
go out there and strive.

00:01:11.212 --> 00:01:14.779
I remember the first $10
million check I ever made,

00:01:14.779 --> 00:01:17.377
and it came in a one
lump $10 million check

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.635
and I gave it to my mother
and I said mom, look,

00:01:19.635 --> 00:01:22.455
because you know I want
my mom to be really proud

00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:25.015
and she said in her broken English,

00:01:25.015 --> 00:01:26.344
hold on a second,

00:01:26.344 --> 00:01:29.920
and she said in her broken English

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:30.753
wonderful

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.749
cause you know she's Hungarian,

00:01:34.749 --> 00:01:39.636
wonderful (speaks in foreign
language) it's Greek.

00:01:39.636 --> 00:01:42.899
Wonderful, now what are you going to do?

00:01:42.899 --> 00:01:44.923
(audience laughs)

00:01:44.923 --> 00:01:47.179
That's precisely the point.

00:01:47.179 --> 00:01:49.143
You did well, now go on.

00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:51.629
If you're the fastest human
being on the face of the planet,

00:01:51.629 --> 00:01:54.407
when all the cameras leave,
and the girls stop kissing you,

00:01:54.407 --> 00:01:56.644
and you put the award away,
are you going to get up

00:01:56.644 --> 00:02:00.603
the next morning, when the
sun is just coming up and

00:02:00.603 --> 00:02:04.329
all by yourself, try to
break your own record

00:02:04.329 --> 00:02:07.208
even though you're the fastest on earth?

00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:10.605
The idea is shouldn't
life be about striving.

00:02:10.605 --> 00:02:12.448
There is no such a thing as winning.

00:02:12.448 --> 00:02:14.912
There's only doing better
than you did before.

00:02:14.912 --> 00:02:18.029
'Cause once you give up,
you're just waiting to die.

00:02:18.029 --> 00:02:19.465
Staying power means hard work.

00:02:19.465 --> 00:02:23.131
Staying power means everyday you get up,

00:02:23.131 --> 00:02:26.298
and you try to stay ahead of the pack.

00:02:27.195 --> 00:02:29.565
Sort of march to the
beat of your own drummer,

00:02:29.565 --> 00:02:33.148
this notion that music
becomes homogenized,

00:02:34.008 --> 00:02:37.597
in other words, there are
lots of successful rappers

00:02:37.597 --> 00:02:40.073
that have short careers,

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:42.331
because if you can replace
one rapper for another

00:02:42.331 --> 00:02:43.331
you're done.

00:02:44.317 --> 00:02:46.709
The more unique you are in what you do,

00:02:46.709 --> 00:02:49.507
the better your chances of continuing on.

00:02:49.507 --> 00:02:51.914
So when you take a look at
me, sometimes its musical.

00:02:51.914 --> 00:02:54.547
Take a look at a band like AC/DC,

00:02:54.547 --> 00:02:56.718
you hear it, you
immediately know what it is.

00:02:56.718 --> 00:02:58.192
That's what they serve up.

00:02:58.192 --> 00:02:59.888
You want ballads, go to another band.

00:02:59.888 --> 00:03:01.174
They serve up straight up.

00:03:01.174 --> 00:03:02.831
That's what you do.

00:03:02.831 --> 00:03:05.498
KISS serves up spectacle.

00:03:05.498 --> 00:03:06.970
We will not sit around on stage

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:10.394
on a Persian carpet, light the candles,

00:03:10.394 --> 00:03:11.391
and sing about

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:14.495
♫ Oh the flaxen haired lass

00:03:14.495 --> 00:03:16.357
♫ On the English countryside

00:03:16.357 --> 00:03:17.357
kill me now!

00:03:18.277 --> 00:03:19.649
We don't do that.

00:03:19.649 --> 00:03:21.697
You want nice quiet stay
at home with grandma,

00:03:21.697 --> 00:03:25.284
pour another glass of water,
and put her false teeth in it,

00:03:25.284 --> 00:03:27.116
let the spinach rise to the top,

00:03:27.116 --> 00:03:28.651
that ain't what we do.

00:03:28.651 --> 00:03:30.156
We blow stuff up.

00:03:30.156 --> 00:03:33.349
With a drummer and a back beat.

00:03:33.349 --> 00:03:35.704
And don't sing about the secret of life

00:03:35.704 --> 00:03:37.301
'cause there is none.

00:03:37.301 --> 00:03:38.248
Here's the secret of life,

00:03:38.248 --> 00:03:39.765
you're alive and then you're not.

00:03:39.765 --> 00:03:42.907
That's it, that's the secret.

00:03:42.907 --> 00:03:45.987
Be glad you're alive while
you're alive you're allowed to

00:03:45.987 --> 00:03:48.148
shake the world up a little bit.

00:03:48.148 --> 00:03:49.428
And that's what you do.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.716
Rockers are on of the
most important assets

00:03:52.716 --> 00:03:54.468
not detriments, assets,

00:03:54.468 --> 00:03:57.864
partner up with somebody who
knows something you don't.

00:03:57.864 --> 00:04:00.913
In that way, one and one can equal three.

00:04:00.913 --> 00:04:03.003
Hang out with smarter or better looking

00:04:03.003 --> 00:04:05.596
or more successful people than you are.

00:04:05.596 --> 00:04:06.772
They'll take you up.

00:04:06.772 --> 00:04:08.390
- You think Paul Stanley's
better looking than you?

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:10.485
- Paul Stanley's a much
better looking guy than I am.

00:04:10.485 --> 00:04:12.077
Much more creative,

00:04:12.077 --> 00:04:14.528
and knows things I will never know.

00:04:14.528 --> 00:04:17.885
And likewise from myself
in regards to him.

00:04:17.885 --> 00:04:19.247
One and one equals three.

00:04:19.247 --> 00:04:21.814
We've been together over 40 years

00:04:21.814 --> 00:04:23.793
and where we sit now,

00:04:23.793 --> 00:04:26.207
KISS outsells the Beatles and Elvis,

00:04:26.207 --> 00:04:28.469
we have more licensing
and merchandising products

00:04:28.469 --> 00:04:30.296
than almost any band out there,

00:04:30.296 --> 00:04:32.829
which is to say, we have a
KISS golf course in Las Vegas,

00:04:32.829 --> 00:04:35.668
and we're going on a KISS
cruise in about a week.

00:04:35.668 --> 00:04:37.227
When I first came to America,

00:04:37.227 --> 00:04:39.033
of course I couldn't speak any English,

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.878
and I went to see Pinocchio.

00:04:40.878 --> 00:04:43.501
I thought the music was great,
and this little puppet boy,

00:04:43.501 --> 00:04:46.367
I immediately connected
to this Pinocchio kid.

00:04:46.367 --> 00:04:48.458
All of sudden, this little cricket,

00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:52.919
this Jiminy Cricket character
comes in like the Messiah,

00:04:52.919 --> 00:04:56.518
and looks at the movie
screen and starts singing,

00:04:56.518 --> 00:04:58.761
When You Wish Upon A Star,

00:04:58.761 --> 00:05:02.102
♫ Your dreams come true

00:05:02.102 --> 00:05:04.164
I thought he was singing to me.

00:05:04.164 --> 00:05:06.997
Shhh Gene, this is from me to you.

00:05:07.994 --> 00:05:11.003
And I could understand the words enough

00:05:11.003 --> 00:05:12.833
that it doesn't matter who you are,

00:05:12.833 --> 00:05:14.800
your dreams can come true.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.660
- You know, what's right to create for

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.233
in the sense of the merchandising world?

00:05:19.233 --> 00:05:21.922
How do you know what's going
to work and what's not?

00:05:21.922 --> 00:05:22.814
Where the success...

00:05:22.814 --> 00:05:24.098
- You don't, you don't.

00:05:24.098 --> 00:05:26.315
You learn to listen.

00:05:26.315 --> 00:05:27.883
People will tell you what they like

00:05:27.883 --> 00:05:30.883
which is why, there's an interesting

00:05:32.101 --> 00:05:33.831
example of what I'm talking about.

00:05:33.831 --> 00:05:37.998
Steven Spielberg, who I've
met, listened to obviously,

00:05:41.312 --> 00:05:45.313
is the most successful
filmmaker of all time.

00:05:45.313 --> 00:05:47.132
He makes every single one of his movies

00:05:47.132 --> 00:05:49.236
has made at least $100 million.

00:05:49.236 --> 00:05:51.137
Without fail.

00:05:51.137 --> 00:05:52.610
Nobody has equaled that record.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.232
And he's done everything from

00:05:54.232 --> 00:05:56.441
Jewish concentration camp stories to

00:05:56.441 --> 00:05:58.086
aliens from other worlds

00:05:58.086 --> 00:06:00.730
to Color Purple to all kinds of stuff.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:04.147
Every single one made $100 million north.

00:06:05.472 --> 00:06:08.268
What he does is, he makes a movie his way,

00:06:08.268 --> 00:06:10.698
he's also part owner of Dreamworks.

00:06:10.698 --> 00:06:11.968
Nobody's going to tell him what to do,

00:06:11.968 --> 00:06:13.733
how to think, how to edit.

00:06:13.733 --> 00:06:15.096
But he does a strange thing,

00:06:15.096 --> 00:06:18.351
after he gets his movie
exactly the way he wants it,

00:06:18.351 --> 00:06:22.518
he will take his movie and
go to Ypsilanti, Michigan

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:24.914
and he'll sit down with people

00:06:24.914 --> 00:06:26.702
who are completely unqualified

00:06:26.702 --> 00:06:28.762
pretty much to do anything,

00:06:28.762 --> 00:06:31.350
especially to tell him
how to edit his movie,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:35.827
and he will listen to them with
what's wrong with his movie.

00:06:35.827 --> 00:06:37.140
They'll say I didn't like the ending,

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.454
I don't like that person,
I don't like that actor.

00:06:39.454 --> 00:06:41.528
And then he goes back and he changes it.

00:06:41.528 --> 00:06:43.893
He listens to the most unqualified people

00:06:43.893 --> 00:06:47.333
because ultimately you,
PBS, KISS, every body

00:06:47.333 --> 00:06:48.624
is in one business.

00:06:48.624 --> 00:06:50.291
The people business.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.479
And no matter what we think of them,

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.312
whether they're the great American

00:06:58.219 --> 00:07:00.380
populist or the unwashed masses,

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:03.182
you can make any point
of reference you like,

00:07:03.182 --> 00:07:06.138
they're the bosses, we just work here.

00:07:06.138 --> 00:07:08.875
This history of KISS, pretty much

00:07:08.875 --> 00:07:10.580
started like any other band.

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.416
Four knuckleheads off
the streets of New York

00:07:12.416 --> 00:07:14.088
who had big dreams of becoming,

00:07:14.088 --> 00:07:15.899
sort of the American version of

00:07:15.899 --> 00:07:18.711
The Beatles on steroids.

00:07:18.711 --> 00:07:22.121
I was always trained as a
young child to go to school

00:07:22.121 --> 00:07:25.314
and to learn and to read voraciously,

00:07:25.314 --> 00:07:27.316
even subjects I wasn't interested in.

00:07:27.316 --> 00:07:29.355
So when we first started
putting the band together

00:07:29.355 --> 00:07:32.357
I read Billboard magazine,
a Record World, a Cashbox,

00:07:32.357 --> 00:07:36.381
the weekly bibles of
the business of music.

00:07:36.381 --> 00:07:39.304
And if you believe in full
disclosure in advertising,

00:07:39.304 --> 00:07:41.331
it says so right away, it says

00:07:41.331 --> 00:07:42.927
music business.

00:07:42.927 --> 00:07:44.703
It doesn't just say music,

00:07:44.703 --> 00:07:47.223
so I recognized that it was
a business and I was curious.

00:07:47.223 --> 00:07:48.056
How does it work?

00:07:48.056 --> 00:07:49.182
What's the price of goods?

00:07:49.182 --> 00:07:50.328
Where's the profit margin?

00:07:50.328 --> 00:07:52.362
What's the distribution method?

00:07:52.362 --> 00:07:53.942
Who, what, when, where and how.

00:07:53.942 --> 00:07:56.927
My mother continues to be
the greatest inspiration

00:07:56.927 --> 00:07:59.728
which is if you take away all your stuff

00:07:59.728 --> 00:08:03.311
could you do it again
in a different field?

00:08:04.275 --> 00:08:08.053
So, I'm in a band, and I
have a restaurant chain,

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:12.078
called Rock and Brews which
is in Los Angeles, and

00:08:12.078 --> 00:08:16.577
Nashville, Kansas City, Maui,
Cabo, every it's exploding,

00:08:16.577 --> 00:08:18.154
and I own a football team,

00:08:18.154 --> 00:08:20.613
the only one in Los
Angeles called LA KISS,

00:08:20.613 --> 00:08:24.655
we're on CBS Sports,
ESPN, and all that stuff.

00:08:24.655 --> 00:08:26.623
Branding, licensing, merchandising,

00:08:26.623 --> 00:08:29.479
KISS is celebrating our 40th anniversary,

00:08:29.479 --> 00:08:31.300
(applause)

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:33.217
and boy do I look good.

00:08:34.953 --> 00:08:36.081
We continue to tour the world.

00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:38.734
I leave Friday from New
York and go to Mexico City

00:08:38.734 --> 00:08:40.783
where we're going to be
playing the stadium there.

00:08:40.783 --> 00:08:42.798
The day after, I go to Phoenix to continue

00:08:42.798 --> 00:08:45.572
with Me, Inc promotions stuff

00:08:45.572 --> 00:08:47.803
then hop on to the Bahamas
for the KISS cruise

00:08:47.803 --> 00:08:51.509
where 4,000 or 5,000
crazy KISS fans pay about

00:08:51.509 --> 00:08:53.222
five grand a piece.

00:08:53.222 --> 00:08:57.103
Let me see, that's $20 to $25
million gross, we take 70%.

00:08:57.103 --> 00:09:00.161
(chuckles)

00:09:00.161 --> 00:09:02.994
And then I go into a Vegas residency,

00:09:02.994 --> 00:09:05.581
in other words, the band
would be enough for anybody.

00:09:05.581 --> 00:09:09.656
I'm voracious, that's a
big word like gymnasium,

00:09:09.656 --> 00:09:12.782
I want to read everything, I want to learn

00:09:12.782 --> 00:09:14.949
stuff I don't know because

00:09:16.952 --> 00:09:21.119
the mouse when it first starts
to learn how the maze works

00:09:22.092 --> 00:09:24.044
is alive, 'cause you don't
know where you're going

00:09:24.044 --> 00:09:26.876
and it's the hunt not the kill,

00:09:26.876 --> 00:09:28.720
and that's a killer mouse that's

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.215
going to finally gets to the cheese.

00:09:31.215 --> 00:09:34.222
Now unless that maze continues to change,

00:09:34.222 --> 00:09:35.761
that mouse is going to take its time

00:09:35.761 --> 00:09:39.081
and get fat bloated and lazy
and finally get to the cheese

00:09:39.081 --> 00:09:41.113
because it knows where it's going.

00:09:41.113 --> 00:09:43.014
Give me a new maze everyday,

00:09:43.014 --> 00:09:44.816
I don't want to get,

00:09:44.816 --> 00:09:47.339
I don't want to lose my
killer instinct, you know.

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:50.573
So every day, as far as I'm concerned,

00:09:50.573 --> 00:09:54.118
should be a new Me, Inc,
new Me Incorporated,

00:09:54.118 --> 00:09:55.862
because I am the business.

00:09:55.862 --> 00:09:56.792
- [Male] What would you say your most

00:09:56.792 --> 00:09:59.125
profitable venture is right now?

00:09:59.125 --> 00:10:02.984
- My most profitable
venture is Gene Simmons.

00:10:02.984 --> 00:10:04.252
- Investing in yourself.

00:10:04.252 --> 00:10:05.324
- Yes.

00:10:05.324 --> 00:10:07.384
Know your product well, they say.

00:10:07.384 --> 00:10:09.343
I invest in myself.

00:10:09.343 --> 00:10:12.876
I never use capital to
invest in other areas.

00:10:12.876 --> 00:10:14.415
I mean, I'm in the stock market and so on,

00:10:14.415 --> 00:10:16.044
but I'm very conservative.

00:10:16.044 --> 00:10:18.138
But with myself?

00:10:18.138 --> 00:10:19.390
Anything I'm passionate about,

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:21.473
I'll throw capital at and

00:10:22.444 --> 00:10:24.908
any new venture I'm involved
in, I'm totally committed

00:10:24.908 --> 00:10:27.218
to, because I know I
never look at the clock.

00:10:27.218 --> 00:10:29.752
- How do you juggle the acting
and the musical careers?

00:10:29.752 --> 00:10:31.876
Which takes precedent?

00:10:31.876 --> 00:10:33.376
- I don't think...

00:10:34.582 --> 00:10:36.554
I take precedent.

00:10:36.554 --> 00:10:38.282
Whether it's now or later,

00:10:38.282 --> 00:10:40.105
there's time to do everything.

00:10:40.105 --> 00:10:43.606
A lot of people don't
understand it, but that's okay.

00:10:43.606 --> 00:10:46.450
Because other people don't have...

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:48.263
They have limited visions, limited dreams.

00:10:48.263 --> 00:10:50.824
People sometimes only want
to be a successful doctor,

00:10:50.824 --> 00:10:52.696
that's all I want to be doctor.

00:10:52.696 --> 00:10:55.647
Well I want...I want it, I want it all.

00:10:55.647 --> 00:10:58.138
- You went to school
in South Williamsburg.

00:10:58.138 --> 00:10:59.338
Have you been back recently?

00:10:59.338 --> 00:11:02.222
- Oh I did worse than school
there, I went to yeshiva.

00:11:02.222 --> 00:11:03.455
(audience laughs)

00:11:03.455 --> 00:11:05.202
I was a hasidic Jew.

00:11:05.202 --> 00:11:07.055
You know ha-see-dem but
I don't believe 'em.

00:11:07.055 --> 00:11:09.418
(chuckles)

00:11:09.418 --> 00:11:12.982
Yeah, I know I don't look
like I come from Sweden,

00:11:12.982 --> 00:11:15.117
but when I first came to America,

00:11:15.117 --> 00:11:17.477
my mother wisely wanted
to keep me off the streets

00:11:17.477 --> 00:11:20.339
because in Williamsburg there
was the Williamsburg Dragons

00:11:20.339 --> 00:11:23.039
and it was a street gang made up of guys

00:11:23.039 --> 00:11:24.958
and I'd never heard of
Christ or anything like that

00:11:24.958 --> 00:11:27.269
and I started in broken English and stuff.

00:11:27.269 --> 00:11:30.920
At night if I stayed out
there longer than 10 pm

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.237
I'd hear Christ-killer,

00:11:33.237 --> 00:11:34.878
never heard of Christ, didn't know

00:11:34.878 --> 00:11:36.803
who what they were talking about

00:11:36.803 --> 00:11:39.280
but they were coming after me.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.405
You know, trying to do some harm

00:11:41.405 --> 00:11:44.088
just because of my religious beliefs.

00:11:44.088 --> 00:11:45.224
You know, I was a Jew.

00:11:45.224 --> 00:11:47.765
It wasn't popular then,
still not a popular thing.

00:11:47.765 --> 00:11:51.107
But by the way, it's not
popular to be a woman.

00:11:51.107 --> 00:11:52.210
Everybody picks on you.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.850
It's not popular to be black, Hispanic,

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:57.101
we all have our crosses to bear.

00:11:57.101 --> 00:11:58.540
So (bleep) what?

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.540
Get over it.

00:12:00.464 --> 00:12:02.074
Get over it.

00:12:02.074 --> 00:12:03.174
Cry over there.

00:12:03.174 --> 00:12:05.287
There's a puddle of water,
every body takes their turn

00:12:05.287 --> 00:12:07.311
to say I was a (mumbles)
and every body picked on me.

00:12:07.311 --> 00:12:08.213
You're right!

00:12:08.213 --> 00:12:10.010
The world is an unfair place.

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:11.911
It's prejudiced, it's biased.

00:12:11.911 --> 00:12:13.266
He will think, I'm a Jew.

00:12:13.266 --> 00:12:14.260
He's gay.

00:12:14.260 --> 00:12:15.152
(bleep) all of you, okay?

00:12:15.152 --> 00:12:17.235
(laughs)

00:12:19.168 --> 00:12:20.607
Get over it.

00:12:20.607 --> 00:12:24.901
Of course it's tough when
you're black, gay, Jewish,

00:12:24.901 --> 00:12:27.389
you know, like a lot of stuff.

00:12:27.389 --> 00:12:29.986
Then you got a lot of stuff
and you can get over that too.

00:12:29.986 --> 00:12:30.933
(audience laughs)

00:12:30.933 --> 00:12:32.169
Everybody's got their stuff,

00:12:32.169 --> 00:12:34.045
at least America gives you a shot.

00:12:34.045 --> 00:12:36.206
In this biased, racist world,

00:12:36.206 --> 00:12:38.828
we have an African-American president.

00:12:38.828 --> 00:12:39.860
So you can do anythi...

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.504
We may even have a female
president next time.

00:12:42.504 --> 00:12:45.713
So, cry to your mommy, I
don't really give a (bleep).

00:12:45.713 --> 00:12:48.163
Just get out there and

00:12:48.163 --> 00:12:51.166
you know the military's
got a great phrase.

00:12:51.166 --> 00:12:55.333
Shame on you if you don't get
up and be all that you can be.

00:12:56.232 --> 00:12:59.129
Can you imagine if you don't
live up to your potential?

00:12:59.129 --> 00:13:02.344
And I guarantee you that
there's greater greatness in you

00:13:02.344 --> 00:13:03.933
than you ever imagined,

00:13:03.933 --> 00:13:06.359
'cause once upon a time,
when you were a little child,

00:13:06.359 --> 00:13:08.443
did you ever, I'm making it up,

00:13:08.443 --> 00:13:09.792
you're making $100 grand a year,

00:13:09.792 --> 00:13:13.243
did you ever envision more than that?

00:13:13.243 --> 00:13:14.326
Okay, $300...

00:13:17.001 --> 00:13:20.504
$100 million a day, I don't know.

00:13:20.504 --> 00:13:22.564
But could you ever imagine,
when you were a kid?

00:13:22.564 --> 00:13:23.583
You couldn't imagine.

00:13:23.583 --> 00:13:27.204
If I found a dollar on
the floor, so perception

00:13:27.204 --> 00:13:30.006
of wealth, and how you're doing in life,

00:13:30.006 --> 00:13:32.941
is all based on where you are
and what you can perceive.

00:13:32.941 --> 00:13:36.338
And I'm telling you that the
future can be so much bigger

00:13:36.338 --> 00:13:37.880
and so much greater for you.

00:13:37.880 --> 00:13:40.038
- Thank you so much for watching us.

00:13:40.038 --> 00:13:42.907
We made this video because
partner office asked us to.

00:13:42.907 --> 00:13:45.177
If there's someone you'd
like us to profile next

00:13:45.177 --> 00:13:47.248
please let us know in the comments below

00:13:47.248 --> 00:13:48.825
and we'll see what we can do.

00:13:48.825 --> 00:13:51.197
- We'd also love to know
which one of Gene Simmons'

00:13:51.197 --> 00:13:53.682
Top Ten Rules meant the most to you.

00:13:53.682 --> 00:13:55.102
Leave it in the comments below and

00:13:55.102 --> 00:13:56.381
we'll join the discussion.

00:13:56.381 --> 00:13:57.618
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:13:57.618 --> 00:14:01.368
Continue to believe,
and we'll see you soon.

